## Slot events: drop NULL-key rows; keep classify and emitters consistent
================================================================================

Context: Review fix round 1 of the SlotProjectionCompiler. A source row with a
NULL key column cannot form a subject URI and would create orphan slots that
the AUTO CDC `KEYS` equality can never match or delete. Separately, `classify`
could call a mapping row-local that the emitters then rejected (an entity
without `class_uri`, a relationship without `predicate`), aborting `compile`.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/SlotProjectionCompiler.py
   `slot_event_view_sql` appends `WHERE <key> IS NOT NULL` after the
   `LATERAL VIEW ... s AS predicate, object` line, one term per source-key column
   (every column of a composite subject template, ANDed; the subject column of a
   relationship); the docstring states that such rows are dropped on purpose.
   A new `_key_columns` helper feeds both `source_key_expr` and the guard so they
   cannot drift. `classify` now delegates to `_batch_reason` and returns `batch`
   (logging the reason at debug level) for an entity without `class_uri` or a
   relationship without `predicate`, so every row-local mapping compiles.
2. tests/units/streaming/test_slot_projection_compiler.py
   New `TestNullKeyGuard` (single key, composite key, relationship, guard matches
   `source_key`) and `TestClassifyAgreesWithEmitters` (the two new batch cases,
   debug log reason, `compile` routing, an agreement matrix over 22 mapping
   shapes asserting that row-local implies the emitters and `compile` succeed).
3. docs/architecture.md
   One sentence on the NULL-key guard in the slot projection subsection.

