## Translator incremental mode and MaterializedViewBuilder (Layer 2)
================================================================================

Context: Task 3 of incremental triple materialization. `_data` and `_graph`
become materialized views that Enzyme can refresh incrementally. Enzyme cannot
refresh a `stack()` generator or a bare `SELECT DISTINCT`, so the translator
learns an Enzyme-safe shape for the triple-set queries, and a new builder
produces the standalone-MV DDL (`CREATE OR REPLACE MATERIALIZED VIEW`, created
from a SQL warehouse; `CREATE OR REFRESH` is pipeline-only). The default output
of the translator is byte-for-byte unchanged. SparqlTranslator sat exactly on
its size-ratchet baseline, so the SQL assembly moved into a new class first.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/TripleSQLAssembler.py (new)
   `unpivot_select`, `build_with_clause`, `finalize_generic_triples` and
   `parse_select_clause`, moved out of SparqlTranslator verbatim; SparqlTranslator
   keeps one-line delegating wrappers under the old private names, so no caller
   or test changed. Re-exported from `back.core.w3c.sparql`.
2. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlTranslator.py, src/back/core/w3c/sparql/__init__.py
   `translate_sparql_to_spark` (class method and package wrapper) gain
   keyword-only `incremental: bool = False` and `mappings_filter:
   Optional[Callable[[dict], bool]] = None`. `incremental` is threaded down to
   the unpivot (a parenthesised `UNION ALL` of single-predicate SELECTs instead
   of `stack()`, `WHERE` repeated per branch) and to the final projection
   (`GROUP BY subject, predicate, object` on the outer query instead of
   `SELECT DISTINCT`, after the `object IS NOT NULL AND TRIM(object) != ''`
   filter and before `LIMIT`; non-distinct queries are left alone). It covers
   the generic and type-constrained paths and the filtered CTE path; the
   join-based builder is unaffected. `mappings_filter` restricts the entity and
   relationship mappings before any branch or CTE is emitted.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py (new), delta/__init__.py
   `data_mv_sql` (slots side with the blank-object filter, UNION ALL the
   parenthesised batch branch, outer GROUP BY, `sha2(object, 256) AS
   object_hash`, `CLUSTER BY`, `REFRESH POLICY`, preview TBLPROPERTIES; either
   side optional, `ValidationError` when both are absent), `graph_mv_sql`,
   `explain_sql`, `refresh_sql`, `refresh_technique_sql`, `plan_is_incremental`,
   `apply` and `last_refresh_technique` (parses `executed as <TECHNIQUE>`,
   `UNKNOWN` on anything else, never raises). The refresh policy is checked
   against AUTO / INCREMENTAL / INCREMENTAL STRICT / FULL because it is inlined.
   The slots table is an AUTO CDC SCD TYPE 1 target (physical deletes, no
   `deleted` column), so the slots side has no tombstone filter; the outer
   GROUP BY collapses the attribute copies that classes sharing a TriplesMap
   each emit; the TRIM filter stays in the slots select because attribute
   objects are COALESCEd to '' rather than NULL.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py
   `build_ensure_inferred_sql` now creates `_inferred` with row tracking and
   deletion vectors (the graph MV unions it, and Enzyme needs row tracking to read
   it incrementally); new `build_enable_row_tracking_sql` is the `ALTER TABLE ...
   SET TBLPROPERTIES` for companions that already exist. `apply` runs it after
   `ensure_inferred_table`. Statement order: optional DROP TABLE `_data`, DROP VIEW
   `_data`, DROP VIEW `_graph`, data MV, ensure `_inferred`, ALTER `_inferred`,
   graph MV (the DROP VIEW `_data` is the review fix recorded at the end).
5. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py
   `slots_table_fqn` and the `_slots` suffix, included in `graph_leaf_suffixes()`
   so `strip_graph_leaf_suffix` handles it.
6. tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_translator_incremental.py (new)
   Default-output snapshots captured before the refactor (all-triples, LIMIT,
