## Fix: MaterializedViewBuilder.apply drops a pre-existing `_data` VIEW
================================================================================

Context: Review fix round 1 of Task 3. `materialize.apply_data_relation` creates
`_data` as a plain VIEW for view-mode Lakehouse domains, and `CREATE OR REPLACE
MATERIALIZED VIEW` cannot replace a VIEW, so such a domain could never enter
incremental mode (every fallback to full re-creates the view).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py
   `apply` always runs a best-effort `materialize.drop_relation(..., kind="view")`
   on `_data` before creating the data MV, next to the optional DROP TABLE kept
   behind `drop_existing_table`. Sequence: [DROP TABLE `_data`] -> DROP VIEW
   `_data` -> DROP VIEW `_graph` -> data MV -> ensure `_inferred` -> ALTER
   `_inferred` -> graph MV. Documented in the docstring.
2. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_materialized_view_builder.py
   Statement-order tests updated; new tests for the unconditional view drop and
   the still-conditional table drop.

