## Lakehouse//RT guardrail routing for Delta graph reads
================================================================================

Context: Task 7 of incremental triple materialization (spec layer 3a). Graph
reads already use a separate query warehouse, optionally a Lakehouse//RT one
(`graph_engine_config.lakehouse.use_sea`). RT enforces guardrails (2-minute
runtime, 300 GB shuffle, statement timeout), so a heavy traversal such as the
recursive BFS could fail on RT although the build warehouse would answer it.
`DeltaFlatStore.execute_query`, the single read entry point, now retries such a
refused statement once on the build warehouse. The query/build warehouse
plumbing itself is reused unchanged.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   New module constant `RT_FALLBACK_MARKERS` (guardrail, exceeds,
   statement_timeout, query timed out, 501, lakehouse//rt, not supported on
   this warehouse). `execute_query` retries once on a lazily created build
   client (`create_databricks_client(domain, settings, for_write=True)`, cached
   in `_fallback_client`) when the lower-cased error contains a marker, logs a
   warning with the SQL length and first 120 characters, and keeps the graph
   statement timeout on both warehouses (shared `_run_read` helper). Other
   errors, unbound stores (`domain=None`) and a missing fallback client
   re-raise the original exception. New read-only `last_read_route`
   (`"query"` | `"build-fallback"`) records which path answered.
2. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_read_warehouse_routing.py (new)
   22 tests: guardrail error retried once on the build client
   (`for_write=True`) with `last_read_route == "build-fallback"`, every marker
   triggers the fallback, the fallback client is cached, non-marked errors
   propagate without creating it, success never touches it, unbound store and
   missing client re-raise the original error, the route is read-only and
   resets after a later success, and the statement timeout is preserved on both
   warehouses.
3. documentation/incremental-materialization.md (new)
   Title plus the Lakehouse//RT subsection (`_graph` is a materialized view in
   incremental/microbatch modes so RT can read it; guardrail fallback to the
   build warehouse; `last_read_route`). A marker comment is left for the rest
   of the document.

