## Fix: keep caller identity on the Lakehouse//RT fallback and retry reads only
================================================================================

Context: Review fix round 1 of Task 7. The fallback built its client with
`for_write=True`, which switches to the service-principal build credentials and
drops the caller's OBO token, so Unity Catalog governance did not apply to the
retried read. It also retried any statement carrying a marker error, including
writes.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaBase.py
   `create_databricks_client` takes a keyword-only `warehouse_id`. On the read
   branch it replaces `resolve_delta_warehouse_id(...)` and forces
   `use_sea=False` (the build warehouse is classic Thrift); host/token
   resolution including the OBO override and cloud-fetch handling are unchanged.
   Ignored when `for_write=True`.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   The fallback client is now `create_databricks_client(domain, settings,
   for_write=False, warehouse_id=resolve_build_warehouse_id(...))`. No retry
   (the original error is re-raised) when the build warehouse id is empty or
   equals the primary client's `warehouse_id`. Only statements starting with
   SELECT or WITH (after whitespace and `--` / `/* */` comments) are retried;
   INSERT/MERGE/DELETE/DDL propagate unchanged and create no client.
   `last_read_route` is reset to `"query"` at the start of every
   `execute_query`, so a failed read never reports a stale route.
3. documentation/incremental-materialization.md
   `_data` (not `_graph`) becomes the materialized view RT reads; `_graph` stays
   a union view for now. Subsection trimmed to 14 lines, with a TODO comment to
   cite the Lakehouse//RT guardrail values.
4. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_base.py,
   tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_read_warehouse_routing.py
   Override tests (warehouse swapped, OBO token kept, `use_sea` False,
   cloud-fetch kept, ignored for writes) and routing tests (factory called with
   `for_write=False` and the build warehouse id, same-warehouse and empty-id
   cases do not retry, write statements propagate, comment/whitespace noise,
   stale route reset). 43 routing tests.

